# ai-bin telemetry fallback. When the Stafficy app is unreachable, `ai` writes its
# telemetry row to a local file instead of the server, and the path it picks walks UP
# from the caller's cwd looking for a dir containing `ai-bin`. There is none above this
# repo, so it falls back to cwd and drops an untracked ai-files/logs/ here.
# An identical file blocked a brewshot land hours after the outage that wrote it
# (brewshot/389, RFC stafficy/14117). The PRIMARY fix is the executable anchor landed at
# b41efbbf3 (plan 17094c94): `ai` resolves its telemetry root from its own location
# rather than from the caller's cwd, so it holds for every invocation. Pinning
# STAFFICY_AI_TELEMETRY_LOG in the ai-bin wrappers is the WEAKER second layer — a wrapper
# pin only reaches callers who go THROUGH a wrapper, and the bare `ai` binary does not;
# that was demonstrated with a shipped binary still littering a foreign cwd while the
# pinned wrapper stayed clean. This line is the last layer, covering anything else that
# ever writes under that root.
ai-files/
